# Seeds the deploy applies, in this order.
#
# `scripts/deploy.sh` reads this file. A seed in db/seed/ that is NOT
# listed here is never applied to production — that is how the test
# fixtures stay out, by omission rather than by a name convention someone
# has to remember.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. Rule seeds expire what they supersede before inserting,
# so replaying them out of sequence would leave the wrong version live.
# This is the order they were originally applied in. Append new seeds at
# the end of their section; do not reorder existing lines.
#
# Every file here must be idempotent — deterministic ids plus
# ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE — because the deploy re-applies a seed whenever
# its contents change.

